      <h2 id="doctor">When to see a doctor</h2>

      <p>
        Low bone density is silent until something breaks, which is why these signs matter more than
        how you feel. Book an appointment rather than starting a supplement if you have:
      </p>

      <ul>
        <li>A fracture from a minor fall or knock, particularly at the wrist, hip or spine — this is the single most important sign.</li>
        <li>Height loss, a developing stoop, or new mid-back pain that came on without an injury.</li>
        <li>Early menopause, or periods that stopped well before the usual age.</li>
        <li>Long-term steroid use, thyroid or parathyroid disease, coeliac disease, inflammatory bowel disease, or bariatric surgery.</li>
        <li>A parent who fractured a hip, or your own history of two or more fractures as an adult.</li>
        <li>A known vitamin D deficiency, or an eating pattern that has kept you underweight.</li>
      </ul>

      <p>
        Osteoporosis has approved medical treatments with fracture-reduction evidence behind them.
        No supplement, including ours, is an alternative to that conversation.
      </p>

